<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13473"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, May 05, 2005 - 10:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He may pretend to be insane. <BR>But those who know can see the lies.  <BR>The game was fun, in torture, his power, <BR> he cared not, for his victims lives. <BR>It took the most important things we treasured, replacing them with pain, with fear. <BR>He treated people like dogs he slaughtered,  <BR>tossing their futures, their families aside. <BR>For that, He deserves no better, <BR> no sorrow, no hope,  <BR>no release from his cell. <BR>I hope the walls around him, are closing in, <BR>and that it&#39;s the last thing he sees <BR>when they take him to hell. <BR> <BR>There that is my poem for the day. Sheila<!--/Text--></td></tr>
